1.What is the difference between origin and upstream?
origin
Usually points to your own fork or the repository you cloned from.
It is the default remote created when you run:


upstream
Usually points to the original repository from which your fork was created.
You generally pull changes from upstream to keep your fork updated.
You typically do not push directly to upstream (unless you have write access).

2.What is the difference between git fetch and git pull?
git fetch downloads the latest changes from the remote repository and updates remote-tracking branches, but it does not modify my current branch. git pull performs a fetch followed by a merge (or rebase), automatically bringing those changes into my working branch
